{
  "kanji": "似",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 似\ntitle: resemble\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 7\nradical: 人\nradicalNumber: 9\nonyomi: [ジ]\nkunyomi: [に.る, ひ.る]\ndistractors: [以, 代, 住]\n---\n\n# 似 — resemble\n\n**Strokes:** 7 · **Key (radical):** 人 (as 亻, no. 9) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n似 expresses resemblance rather than strict identity.\nWith [似る](../words/似る.md) にる, learners will often need the form 似ている (にている), \"be similar; look alike.\"\n類似 るいじ is a noun for similarity and can also take する.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** find the person-shaped 亻 next to [以](以.md), then imagine comparing two people who look alike.\nThis is a memory story based on the modern shape, not etymology.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| に.る | kun | [似る](../words/似る.md) にる — resemble |\n| ジ | on | 類似 るいじ — similarity |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [似る](../words/似る.md) にる — resemble; take after\n- 類似 るいじ — resemblance; similarity\n\n## Notes\n\nCompare 母に似ている (ははににている), \"resemble one's mother\": に marks the person used for comparison.\n[以](以.md) lacks the extra 亻; [代](代.md) and [住](住.md) have simpler right sides.\nThe canonical radical 人 appears here as 亻.\nSimilarity does not require every feature to be the same.\n",
